The {{Term/Store|Moblin Mask|Moblin Masks|Series, BotW, TotK, AoC}} is a recurring [[Item]] in {{TLoZ Series}}.{{Exp Game|BotW, TotK, AoC}}<ref name="BotW Inventory"/><ref name="TotK Inventory"/><ref name="AoC Allies"/>

==Location and Uses==
==={{BotW|-}}===
{{Descriptions BotW}}
The Moblin Mask is a piece of [[Armor]] that can be purchased from [[Kilton]] at the [[Fang and Bone]] shop for 199 [[Mon]] after freeing one [[Divine Beast]]. It cannot be enhanced by a [[Great Fairy]], nor can it be [[Dye]]d at the [[Kochi Dye Shop]]. When worn, it grants [[Link]] the [[Disguise (Mechanic)|Disguise]] [[Added Effect]], allowing him to blend in with [[Moblin]]s.<ref name="BotW Inventory"/> However, the Moblin Mask does not prevent other [[Enemy|Enemies]] in the same area from attacking Link. It also makes quiet Moblin sounds as Link moves around. While wearing the Moblin Mask, Link adopts a new idle pose to match that of a Moblin.

==={{TotK|-}}===
{{Descriptions TotK}}
The Moblin Mask returns in {{TotK|-}}, functioning the same as it did in {{BotW|-}}. It can be obtained from [[Koltin's Stall]] for two [[Bubbul Gem]]s after completing "[[The Hunt for Bubbul Gems!]]" and "[[The Search for Koltin]]". Subsequent Moblin Masks can be purchased from [[Cece]] for 4000 [[Rupee]]s.

==Other Appearances==
==={{AoC|-}}===
{{Noncanon|Start}}
{{Descriptions AoC}}
The Moblin Mask is a piece of [[Attire]] that can only be worn by [[Link]], and is obtained when the [[Warrior]]s complete the [[Quest#Hyrule Warriors: Age of Calamity|Quest]] "[[Cold Desert Nights]]". The mask was made by the merchant of [[Fang and Bone]] to replicate an actual [[Moblin]].<ref name="AoC Allies"/>
{{Noncanon|End}}

